WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.250
Speaker 1: One of the sort of side stories
with what's going on on Twitter with this

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:10.160
reportedly accepted offer for Elon Musk to
purchase Twitter and to take it private.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.889
One of the side stories that's come up and
many of you have emailed me about it, many

00:00:13.889 --> 00:00:19.350
of you have noticed how it has affected my
Twitter account is the significant number

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:24.580
of followers that many left leaning accounts
have lost on Twitter.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:30.220
And so I'm going to explain this story as
I currently know it, and I'm going to try

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:35.730
to be as accurate and precise as possible
without going beyond what we know and what's

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.930
been said, because it is still sort of a developing
story.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:44.600
So the way that this started is right around
Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, when we learned about

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.230
this effort that has reportedly been accepted
by Twitter, although it's not yet been approved.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:53.230
It's been accepted in principle, but it's
not hasn't happened and it still may not.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:59.240
For Elon Musk to buy Twitter, we started seeing
overwhelming anecdotal reports of high profile

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:06.640
Twitter accounts and verified Twitter accounts
reporting losing huge numbers of followers

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:12.180
right in that period of time where it started
to become known that Elon Musk may be buying

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.780
Twitter.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:19.740
And initially the assumption was before Twitter
put out any statement, you saw a lot of venture

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:25.390
capital and investment type people saying
what's happening here is Twitter is cleaning

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:30.289
up the bots and the fake accounts for the
sale.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:32.920
Because part of what you need to this was
the story they were telling.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:33.920
There was no evidence for this.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.530
But they were saying, you know, when you're
going to true, part of the valuation is based

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.920
on the number of users.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:44.050
And so you want to feel really good that you
can give an accurate number of real people

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:45.630
that are using the service.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:48.409
So you want to eliminate bots and fake accounts.

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:53.660
And it may be that the more followers you
have, the more fake followers that you have.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.630
It never struck me as accurate.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:02:02.049
I don't think that just an agreement in principle
would immediately start some kind of algorithmic

00:02:02.049 --> 00:02:05.210
closure of accounts believed to be fake or
bots.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:06.640
So it just wasn't logical.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:12.090
It's possible that would be done, but the
idea that it would start instantly upon the

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.650
news breaking of Elon Musk's purchase, it
just didn't really make any sense.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:16.990
But the numbers were pretty stunning.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:20.631
A former president, Barack Obama, who's one
of the most followed people on Twitter, maybe

00:02:20.631 --> 00:02:22.170
the most followed.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:27.010
He lost more than 300,000 followers after
the announcement on Monday.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:32.390
My verified account, my tiny little teeny
weeny verified account, lost about a thousand

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:39.060
followers in that Monday, Tuesday period between
Sunday and Tuesday, Nancy Pelosi lost like

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.680
13,000 followers.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.160
Elizabeth Warren lost 14,000 followers.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:45.790
Bernie Sanders lost 19,000 followers.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:52.020
But then it appeared that not everybody was
actually losing followers because some right

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:57.280
wing accounts were seeing massive dumps of
new followers come in.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.090
Marjorie Taylor GREENE, the radical Trumpist
congresswoman personally.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:06.220
She's banned on Twitter, but her congressional
account is still active.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:07.220
I know.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.220
Whatever.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.470
That's not even the whether that makes sense
or not.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.490
It's not the issue.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:18.550
Marjorie Taylor Greene's account saw a record
new 100,000 followers over that two day period.

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:20.770
I you know, I lost a thousand.

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:22.640
She gained 100,000.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:27.640
So that can't be because of purging bots,
because some people were gaining followers

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.709
and they seemed to be mostly right wingers.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.900
Well, Twitter has now spoken out about it.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:37.750
Twitter says that the follower changes that
have been observed are coming from, quote,

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.640
natural account terminations.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:45.660
A spokesperson at Twitter who spoke on the
condition of anonymity said the more high

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.980
profile the account, the more of a fluctuation
we've seen.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.819
But these are not bot closures.

00:03:52.819 --> 00:03:56.740
This is just people closing accounts and people
signing up.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:03.120
So the current claim from Twitter is I lost
a thousand followers because a thousand of

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:07.810
my followers were genuinely mad that Elon
Musk is buying Twitter.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:10.670
And so they went and they closed their Twitter
accounts.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:17.430
And at the same time, Marjorie Taylor GREENE
gained 100,000 followers because I guess right

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:23.110
wingers presumably happy that Elon Musk is
buying Twitter, said, I'm going to make a

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:27.259
Twitter account or I'm going to take my dormant
Twitter account and start following people

00:04:27.259 --> 00:04:31.130
like Marjorie Taylor GREENE because I'm ready
for the free speech and all of the different

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:33.449
things that Elon Musk is going to bring.

00:04:33.449 --> 00:04:35.860
Ted Cruz gained more than 50,000 followers.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.900
Matt Gates gained about 25,000 followers.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:45.939
Right wing nut Brazilian President Jair Bolsonaro
gained close to 100,000 followers.

00:04:45.939 --> 00:04:48.249
So do we believe this?

00:04:48.249 --> 00:04:49.370
Do we believe this?

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:54.610
I mean, if it it can't be that this was a
bot purge because the right wing accounts

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:57.100
are gaining followers.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.529
If the belief is.

00:04:58.529 --> 00:04:59.529
These are the.

00:04:59.529 --> 00:05:00.650
Natural reactions.

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:05.530
Leftists are mad about Elon Musk, so they're
closing accounts and right wingers are thrilled

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:06.719
about Elon Musk buying it.

00:05:06.719 --> 00:05:08.680
So they're signing up.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:15.460
If that's the case, it's a concern because
of what it signals that Twitter may become.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:21.960
The other part of it is I mean, listen, it's
striking me as a little bit of a statistical

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:28.789
improbability that you would see such partizan
changes to fall over so quickly.

00:05:28.789 --> 00:05:29.850
It's just kind of weird.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:32.120
We work with algorithms all the time.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.199
And Jenny Yuga tweeted something similar.

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:39.139
We see how these things have happened over
long periods of times on time, on YouTube,

00:05:39.139 --> 00:05:40.960
and on different platforms.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.309
I just don't know that I buy it.

00:05:42.309 --> 00:05:43.309
I don't know.

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:45.779
I'm not accusing anyone in particular of lying.

00:05:45.779 --> 00:05:47.740
Maybe it's a combination of things.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:52.680
And of course, if the explanation that Twitter
is giving is a lie, well, it's a concern that

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:53.680
Twitter is lying.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.339
So to me, this is a red flag either way.

00:05:56.339 --> 00:06:02.419
My personal behavior on Twitter is I continue
to mute every annoying account because Twitter

00:06:02.419 --> 00:06:05.369
has always been filled with lots of right
wing trolls.

00:06:05.369 --> 00:06:08.789
I actually looked at my account the other
day.

00:06:08.789 --> 00:06:14.819
What it would look like without thousands
of trolls muted, it would be completely unusable.

00:06:14.819 --> 00:06:19.680
And what's really funny is there are people
who have been tweeting trash to me on Twitter

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:20.680
for years.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:26.039
They've had no idea that I can't see their
tweets and for years that it made me laugh

00:06:26.039 --> 00:06:27.919
a little bit, that there's so many of them.

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:30.000
But as far as what we know now.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:36.169
Twitter saying the fluctuations, left wingers
losing followers, right wingers gaining followers.

00:06:36.169 --> 00:06:44.199
This is a reflection of natural account creation
and deletion, which, if true, raises real

00:06:44.199 --> 00:06:47.490
questions about what the future of Twitter
looks like under Elon Musk.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:54.250
On today's bonus show, we're going to examine
Elon Musk's history of speech as a defender

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:57.659
or not of free speech, which has been very
much at issue here.

00:06:57.659 --> 00:06:58.759
That'll be on today's bonus show.

